   "1-LOOP EQUALS TORSION FOR TWO-BRIDGE KNOTS"
  ],
  "abstract": "Motivated by the conjectured asymptotics of the Kashaev invariant, Dimofte and the first author introduced a power series associated to a suitable ideal triangulation of a cusped hyperbolic 3-manifold, proved that its constant (1-loop) term is a topological invariant and conjectured that it equals to the adjoint Reidemeister torsion. We prove this conjecture for hyperbolic 2-bridge knots by combining the work of Ohtsuki\u2013Takata with an explicit computation.",
